<% company_name = snapshot.dig("company", "name") %>
<% participation = snapshot["participation"] || {} %>
<% docs_first = snapshot["docs_first_phase"] == true || snapshot["report_kind"].to_s == "baseline" %>
<% base = report_evidence_base(snapshot) %>
<% doc_count = base["documents"].to_i %>
<% evidence_sentence = report_evidence_base_sentence(snapshot) %>
<section class="page">
  <div class="eyebrow">Methodology</div>
  <h1 class="page-title">How we measured</h1>
  <div class="split">
    <div>
      <% if docs_first %>
        <p class="method" style="margin-top:0;">
          This baseline report draws on structured extraction from internal documents for <%= h company_name %>
          <% if doc_count.positive? %>
            (<%= doc_count %> supporting <%= doc_count == 1 ? "document" : "documents" %> cited)
          <% end %>.
          Signals and patterns are produced by structured extraction over the document text; employee interviews can be added later to strengthen the same evidence. Recommendations are matched from those signals against the solution catalog.
          <% if participation["invited"].to_i.positive? && participation["completed"].to_i.zero? %>
            <%= participation["invited"].to_i %> employees have been invited; their interviews will be added as they complete.
          <% end %>
        </p>
      <% else %>
        <p class="method" style="margin-top:0;">
          Findings draw on confidential discovery interviews (WhatsApp and web chat) for <%= h company_name %>. Each interview maps the person's own areas of work, then asks how each works, what gets in the way, and how often and how long it takes.
          <% if participation["invited"].to_i.positive? %>
            <%= participation["completed"].to_i %> of <%= participation["invited"].to_i %> invited employees completed the full discovery flow.
          <% end %>
          <% if doc_count.positive? %>
            Interview evidence is reinforced by <%= doc_count %> internal <%= doc_count == 1 ? "document" : "documents" %>.
          <% end %>
          Findings and this report are reviewed before release, and a finding about a role only one person holds is never included until a consultant has checked it. Signals and patterns are drawn from the same interviews and documents.
        </p>
      <% end %>
    </div>
    <div class="method" style="align-self:center;">
      <dl>
        <dt>How hours are worked out</dt>
        <dd style="font-size:9pt;color:var(--muted);">From how often and how long each person said a piece of work takes, on 48 working weeks, 240 working days and 8-hour days a year. Ranges stay ranges, rounded outward. Waiting on others is never counted, no figure is larger than one person's working year, and nothing is converted to salary. Where two people described the same work, it is counted once.</dd>
        <% if evidence_sentence %>
          <dt>Evidence base</dt>
          <dd style="font-size:9pt;color:var(--muted);"><%= h evidence_sentence.upcase_first %>. Individual interview transcripts, document files and media exhibits are working papers and are deliberately excluded from this deliverable — findings are reported with the weight of evidence behind them, not the source material itself.</dd>
        <% end %>
        <dt>Review</dt>
        <dd style="font-size:9pt;color:var(--muted);">When consultants are assigned, overall notes and section comments are merged into an appendix at platform approval. Live discussions and WhatsApp follow-up threads are collaboration tooling and are intentionally excluded from this deliverable.</dd>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
  <%= render "reports/page_footer", company_name: company_name %>
</section>
